Resolved in 7ad054f0. Both the `skipPrompts` branch and the "accept defaults" branch now do a two-pass write:

```js
// 1. static defaults first so the answer bag is populated
for (const question of questions) {
  if (typeof question.default !== 'function') {
    allAnswers[question.name] = question.default;
  }
}
// 2. function defaults evaluated against the populated bag
for (const question of questions) {
  if (typeof question.default === 'function') {
    try {
      allAnswers[question.name] = question.default(allAnswers);
    } catch (error) {
      await prompts.log.warn(`Could not evaluate dynamic default for ${question.name} under --yes: ${error.message}`);
    }
  }
}
```

`buildQuestion`'s function default closure already reads `answers[${moduleName}_${fieldName}]` as its first lookup, so passing `allAnswers` resolves same-module `{other_key}` placeholders the same way the interactive prompt callback would. Try/catch surfaces resolution failures as warnings instead of crashing the install.

Same fix for the accept-defaults non-`--yes` path, since it had the same `if (typeof question.default === 'function') continue;` skip without a later evaluation.

